  "worked_solution": "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}={a}_{1}\\frac{(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term of the series, and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nTo find $r,$ we find the ratio between the consecutive terms ${a}_{4}$ and ${a}_{5}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{5}}{{a}_{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{81}{2})}{(\\frac{27}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{27} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we must determine the value of ${a}_{1}.$ To do this, we use the formula for the $n$th term, which states that\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nFor $n=4,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{4-1} \\\\ \\frac{27}{2} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{27}{2} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot 27 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, if we substitute ${a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2},N=8$ and $r=3$ into the formula for ${S}_{N},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{8} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1-{3}^{8}}{1-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{-6\\,560}{-2} \\\\  & =1\\,640\\end{aligned}\n$$",
